+# check-change Step 3, Layer 2 - category: memory - PR #780 (issue 777)
+# Grounded only from origin/plan/756/base (git show) and docs/adr at that base. Nothing cited below is added by this diff.
+category: memory
+changed_artifacts:
+  - core/components/memory/standards/rules/pipeline-next.md      # edit-ontology added to meta_exempt
+  - core/components/skills/author-product-ontology/SKILL.md      # reclassified: play-run, user-invocable false, staged
+principles:
+  - id: G1
+    text: "A play that is a meta/bootstrap play, not part of the product pipeline, is listed under meta_exempt and renders no Next line; every user-invocable compiled play must be mapped or exempt."
+    source: "origin/plan/756/base:core/components/memory/standards/rules/pipeline-next.md (header, 'Meta / bootstrap plays' comment); lint_play.py L319-343 at base"
+  - id: G2
+    text: "Skills are never invoked by humans; humans run plays, plays call agents, agents call skills. user-invocable is false for skills."
+    source: "origin/plan/756/base:docs/adr/005-skills-as-capabilities.md ('Invocability Rules: Humans CANNOT invoke skills directly'); base:docs/components/skills.md ('Model-Invocable Only')"
+  - id: G3
+    text: "A skill reads only what its agent puts in short-term memory; the play reads no memory and passes paths; the product-model/ontology write is the work of a play built for it, not a memory write."
+    source: "origin/plan/756/base:docs/adr/039-memory-writes-go-to-short-term-memory-plays-read-no-memory.md (Decision 1 and 2; Amends ADR 009 Rule 3)"
+  - id: G4
+    text: "An agent runs only skills listed in its own pool/capabilities table."
+    source: "origin/plan/756/base:core/components/agents/product-os-keeper.md (Available Skills table, Identity: 'author model artifacts only through your skills')"
+  - id: G5
+    text: "Docs and indexes that name a component's job must match the component."
+    source: "origin/plan/756/base:core/components/memory/standards/templates/_index.md L21; schemas/product-os/_index.md L9; templates/product-ontology.md L5"
+conformant:
+  - file: core/components/memory/standards/rules/pipeline-next.md
+    principle: G1
+    note: "edit-ontology is a harness-maintenance play beside create-play/edit-play/create-loop/edit-loop in meta_exempt; the play is user-invocable and has no successor, so exempting it is what the rule requires. One-line addition, no other change to the map."
+  - file: core/components/skills/author-product-ontology/SKILL.md
+    principle: G2
+    note: "user-invocable true -> false, text now says a person never runs it. This brings the skill into line with ADR 005. The base docs/components/skills.md 'Meta-Utility exception' was an exception to ADR 005 with no ADR behind it; the diff removes it consistently in skills.md."
+  - file: core/components/skills/author-product-ontology/SKILL.md
+    principle: G3
+    note: "Stage drafts are written to the play's working (short-term memory) folder and the ontology edit lands through the change plays (PR), not as a runtime memory write. Consistent with ADR 039 Decision 1."
+findings:
+  - id: M1
+    severity: P2
+    file: core/components/skills/author-product-ontology/SKILL.md
+    principle: G4
+    source: "origin/plan/756/base:core/components/agents/product-os-keeper.md (Available Skills / Intent->Skill table, no author-product-ontology row; base grep for 'ontology' in the agent finds only an unrelated 'ontology v4' note at line 182)"
+    finding: "The skill is now run only through the product-os-keeper agent, and edit-ontology dispatches that agent with it, but the agent's skill pool does not list author-product-ontology and the agent file is not in the diff. The agent's own contract says it authors only through the skills in its pool. Add the skill (used by /edit-ontology) to the agent's table and mapping."
+  - id: M2
+    severity: P3
+    file: core/components/skills/author-product-ontology/SKILL.md
+    principle: G3
+    source: "origin/plan/756/base:docs/adr/039-memory-writes-go-to-short-term-memory-plays-read-no-memory.md (a skill reads only what its agent puts in short-term memory); base:docs/adr/016-agent-json-contract.md (contract carries paths)"
+    finding: "The new Stages section says each stage 'reads the drafts of the stages before it' and may carry `change` and `problems`, but the Input table is unchanged: no `stage`, no draft-path inputs, no `change`, no `problems`, and no Output row for a stage draft. The skill's contract is therefore only defined in the play, so the skill cannot be read on its own. Add these fields to Input/Output. Also the Input default for ontology_path/template_path still points at the installed copy (~/.garura/core/memory/...) that the play overrides with the source path; ADR 039 wants paths handed in, so the default is now misleading."
+  - id: M3
+    severity: P4
+    file: core/components/memory/standards/templates/_index.md, core/components/memory/standards/schemas/product-os/_index.md
+    principle: G5
+    source: "origin/plan/756/base:core/components/memory/standards/templates/_index.md L21 ('Used by: author-product-ontology (skill)'); base:core/components/memory/standards/schemas/product-os/_index.md L9"
+    finding: "These memory indexes (not in the diff) still present author-product-ontology as the way the ontology is built, with no mention that it is run only by /edit-ontology. Not wrong, but now incomplete; a pointer to the play would help. The same holds for core/grounding/glossary.md L67."
+  - id: M4
+    severity: P4
+    file: core/components/memory/standards/rules/pipeline-next.md
+    principle: G1
+    source: "origin/plan/756/base:core/components/memory/standards/rules/pipeline-next.md (intro paragraph names only 'install' style meta plays by comment; 'The flow' lists the Change loop members)"
+    finding: "edit-ontology ends by running commit/propose/check/merge-change (position: both), yet is exempt from the Next line like the other meta plays. That matches the rule; noted only so the reviewer confirms it is intended that its close names no successor."
+grounding_unavailable: []
